<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arabisation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">690s</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arabisation refers to the policy, begun under the Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Abd al-Malik in the 690s, of making Arabic the official language of administration. Government registers previously kept in Greek or Persian were converted into Arabic, and a new Islamic coinage was introduced. The reform strengthened central control and the Arab and Islamic character of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arabisation.jpg" alt="Arabisation" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Reinhard Saczewski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Umayyaden-_Abd_al-Malik_-_M%C3%BCnzkabinett,_Berlin_-_5489972.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
